{"insertText":{"location":{"index":173270,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"text":"Table J7. Robustness of the Ten Significant Architecture Differences\nNote. Supplementary. The ten fixed-recipe SwinFusion++ differences significant after Holm adjustment. Pre-scoring partition: grouping recorded before test scoring. Seed sign agreement: cross-seed pairings with the ensemble ΔAUC sign. DFo global clusters: 175 lineage clusters instead of 201. “< 0.005” = Holm-adjusted p below 0.005; with m = 26 and 27 the smallest attainable values (0.0052 and 0.0054) are printed as 0.005. C23/C40 = FaceForensics++ DeepFakes at compression C23/C40; CDF = Celeb-DF v2; DFo = DeeperForensics-1.0. Delete-one-cluster jackknife standard errors of ΔAUC were 0.99 to 1.32 times the bootstrap standard errors for Celeb-DF v2 targets (mean 1.15; 15 comparisons) and 0.84 to 1.05 times for the other test sets (mean 1.00; 50 comparisons), so Celeb-DF v2 intervals may be narrower than nominal. Across all 15 DeeperForensics-1.0-target comparisons, the 175-cluster re-analysis changed no Holm decision."}},
