{"insertText":{"location":{"index":173222,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"text":"Table J6. Within-Dataset Sensitivity: Detectable Difference and Available Headroom\nNote. Supplementary, post hoc. SE: standard deviation of the 5,000 paired cluster-bootstrap ΔAUC draws. MDD: smallest ΔAUC detectable with 80% power by a two-sided normal-approximation test, (z + 0.84) × SE, with z = 1.96 (α = 0.05) or 2.73 (α = 0.05/8). Headroom: 1 − comparator ROC-AUC, the largest possible gain for SwinFusion++. MDD exceeds headroom in 7 of 8 comparisons at α = 0.05/8. Celeb-DF v2 intervals are approximate: all 843 fake videos lie in 9 identity clusters."}},
